WEBVTT

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.820
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.550
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.160
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.810
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.890
<i>Hey, I'm counting on you.</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.360
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.190
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:16.130
An enemy like that was just like 
a morning workout, wasn't it?

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:17.730
I smell something.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.680
What is it?

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.600
Something smells good.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.580
Ah, so you noticed?

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:26.800
It's this.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.570
I put some herbs in this 
protection charm I made.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.880
I begged Master and they gave me some.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.950
That herb that Hasebe is always watering?!

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.560
There's only one charm 
imbued with this power.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.010
You're not fair!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:48.810
Stop sniffing it!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.360
But it might grant me some kind of blessing.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.520
I have raised Master's herbs with dignity.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.900
I wonder what I could put in mine.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.670
You made one, too, Kiyomitsu?

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.420
It's because I know what will 
be en vogue around here.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.530
As expected.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:15.170
You made yours to cheer yourself up, right?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.890
What's everyone been putting in theirs?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.400
I-I'm scared.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.550
What are you doing?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:33.520
38 - Tachi
 <b>Kousetsu Samonji</b>

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:33.070
I am searing the image of this 
beautiful flower in my memory.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.960
Osayo picked it for you 
this morning, Nii-sama.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:38.820
Right?

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:47.620
<i>Now that Kousetsu Samonji has arrived, 
all three brothers are together.</i>

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.050
<i>Sayo looks happy, too.</i>

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.820
Not yet!

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.740
They're getting stronger.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.750
You're right!

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.800
Yagen's really been looking after them.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.750
Yeah, they're really enthusiastic.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:07.790
There!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.210
<i>I have to guide them.</i>

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.730
Yagen! It's about time.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.110
Whoops, is it that time already?

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.760
Okay, training is over!

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.930
Good work, everybody!

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.140
Today isn't just about sparring.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.530
It's the day you've all been waiting for! 
We're going to the ocean!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.100
All right! Yay!

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.240
Ocean! The ocean!

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:32.950
Let's eat lunch and get ready.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.460
Okay!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.970
The bathing suits Master 
made looks good on you guys!

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.590
You look good, too, Mutsunokami!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.970
This wouldn't suit anyone except me!

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:56.060
Oh, the newbie has come, too?

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:00.320
39 - Wakizashi 
<b>Urashima Kotetsu</b>

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.640
I'm Urashima Kotetsu!

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.590
Won't someone go see Ryuuguu Castle with me?

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.200
I don't really know the way, though!

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.580
You're an interesting fellow!

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.150
I hope you get along with everyone!

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.740
It's nice to meet you!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.610
Nice to meet you, too!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.830
Be careful.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:13.610
Right.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:18.620
It is with the consideration of our Master 
that we are able to go to the ocean now.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.630
Everyone be sure to thank Master!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.940
Master! We'll be heading 
off to the beach now!

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.380
Master, thank you!

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:27.940
Thank you for the bathing suit!

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.500
It's wonderful.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:29.600
Can't you lot be quiet?

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.110
Master has something they 
are trying to look up—

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.210
Ah, don't talk all at once!

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:38.460
Ah, is Master not coming with us?

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.060
You know why.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.000
Master is the indoors type. Now get going.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.690
See you later, Master!

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.090
We'll be going!

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:01.870
It's the ocean!

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.330
All right, the first person to reach 
the ocean is the sharpest!

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:08.670
It's me!

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.110
I'm number one!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.630
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.000
Everyone's in high spirits.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.180
Sunburn is your skin's enemy.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.070
Why did you come to the ocean, then?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.030
To keep you company, of course.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.340
You'd be lonely without me.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.490
Huh, well, thanks for that.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.570
Well, I'm going to head into the 
water, so come keep me company!

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:38.570
H-Hey, wait! At least let
me put on some sunscreen!

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.540
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:43.290
Five.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.480
Six.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.960
Seven.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.800
The water tastes like something.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:52.630
Taste?

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.140
You all try it, too.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.850
<i>So this is what it tastes like.</i>

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.580
<i>It has a metallic taste, but one more time.</i>

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.810
I want to try going to 
that island over there.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.130
Kamekichi! It's the ocean!

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.160
Do you wanna go swimming, too?

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:29.310
I see...

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.190
We can search for Ryuuguu Castle, too!

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:32.380
Urashima-san!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.700
You can talk to the turtle, can't you?

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:35.680
Nope!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.550
He doesn't understand me at all.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:40.440
Ah, Kamekichi! Where are you going?

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.430
Wow, what a cute seashell!

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.220
I should collect some and make a necklace!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.890
Look, Midare.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:51.450
You get numb when this starfish stings you,

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.180
I wonder if it could be an anesthetic?

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.530
I want to take it back home.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:55.310
Look.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.440
That's so creepy.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.760
Hey, stop it!

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.680
Help me, Atsushi!

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.120
Delicious! Wish I had soy sauce!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.850
We can make good money off of this!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:08.380
Ah, will you let me know 
if you see a mitten crab?

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.390
Why don't you do something more fun?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.580
This is my first time seeing the ocean.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:21.430
I did not get out much because I was
 a bird in a cage, kept only as decoration.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:26.390
Souza-niisama, seeing this kind of scenery 
doesn't brighten your mood, does it?

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.820
Kousetsu-niisama...

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.000
I wonder if he's actually having fun...

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:41.190
Mutsunokami-san said we should 
make lots of memories today.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:44.350
I don't have any memories.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:47.550
You can still make memories 
even if you have none, though.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:53.150
You won't need to worry about the past 
once you start making fun memories.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.410
Oh, it went through!

00:08:55.740 --> 00:09:00.230
Handshake! This feeling! 
This is a memory, too.

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.680
I haven't put my hand in yet.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.180
Then, what did I just touch?

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.440
Turtle!

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.120
Kamekichi!

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:16.250
I wonder if the Shinsengumi 
played in the ocean, too.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:17.580
Of course not.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.150
What if the anti-shogunate faction
 had seen them playing in the water?

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.030
It was that kind of era.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.410
That's true.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.430
I dropped my sunscreen.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.240
Say, Yasusada, won't you go get it for me?

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.810
Get it yourself.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:40.750
Okita-kun would have gotten it
for me if I asked because he was kind.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.540
Jeez, I guess I have no choice.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.680
One bold Okita strike!

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:54.890
Here is your memory.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.910
What is this?

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.060
Isn't it pretty?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.160
Here.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.750
Would you like some tea?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.870
Thank you.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.510
The ocean is fun, isn't it?

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:29.390
Osayo, you are getting better.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.780
Those brothers get along well, don't they?

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.020
What's the matter?

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:56.080
That's right! I brought watermelon! 
Why don't we all eat it together?

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:57.440
S-Sure.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.770
Are you all having fun, too?

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.420
Something the matter?

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.980
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.680
Did you enjoy the ocean?

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.640
Yeah, I guess.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.080
It was a lot of fun.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:24.370
I-I'm writing about the ocean today 
in my journal so I can tell Ichi-nii.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.450
Well?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.640
Isn't it pretty?

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.600
I'm making a necklace to give to Ichi-nii.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.820
I'm going to give him star sand, too.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.280
It's like their feelings of
 wanting to see Ichi-nii

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.290
have only increased after going to the ocean.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.010
I see.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:45.760
This is far better than keeping their 
desire to see him secret in their hearts.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:39.550
Yagen.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:44.920
Are you awake?

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.350
I guess.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:51.300
Ichigo Hitofuri isn't showing up very easily.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.310
That's true.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:59.730
Seeing all the Awataguchi swords, I can't 
help but think it'd be nice if he'd come soon.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.560
They've been waiting so 
long for their brother.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:10.180
<b>For Ichi-nii</b>

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:10.180
<b>Journal</b>

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:16.300
Dwelling on it must be painful.

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:17.710
But...

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.870
Isn't caring for someone a happy thing?

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:28.460
It might be painful now, but caring for 
Ichigo Hitofuri is also a happy thing,

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:32.860
because that means one day, it will
 all be turned into good memories.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.840
It was the same for me.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.690
Good night.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.970
<b>Prayer</b>

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.970
<b>Fuji</b>

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:05.060
Yagen, we received an talisman imbued 
with strong powers from Master.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:07.820
Come.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.340
I am Ichigo Hitofuri,

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.980
the only tachi made by 
Awataguchi Yoshimitsu.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:21.770
I will do my utmost to fulfill my 
duties for my master and the citadel.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.140
Understood, I will follow you.

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:34.710
I-Ichi-nii!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:41.440
40 - Tachi
 <b>Ichigo Hitofuri</b>

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.510
We finally meet, Yagen Toushirou.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.430
No, Yagen.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.340
I'll put the bell on for you.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:47.900
Thank you.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:55.100
I have a nice spot I want to take 
you to. Will you come with me?

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.120
A nice spot?

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:10.860
This is the best view in the whole citadel.

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:12.080
Is that so?

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.590
The wind feels nice.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.280
It's pretty big, isn't it?

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.690
There's an outdoor bath and 
a laundry room, too.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:24.870
The fields are over there, 
and that huge building there

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.770
is the training hall where we train daily.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:29.780
We've gotten much stronger.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.270
That is a fine tree over there.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.590
It is.

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:39.420
It's the symbol of this citadel.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:43.590
At first, we didn't know what kind of tree 
it was, but it blossomed into a cherry tree.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.100
It was very beautiful.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.650
I hope we'll be able to see it
 bloom together next time.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.360
That would be nice.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.140
Yagen, what is that thing 
hanging around your neck?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.400
Ah, this?

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:03.550
It's been popular around the citadel lately.
It's a protection charm I made myself.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:05.010
Protection charm?

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.530
May I see it?

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:12.040
That cherry tree is a tree 
that grants wishes.

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:17.150
I don't know who wrote 
that one, but it seems that

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:20.690
everyone wrote about Ichi-nii 
and attached it to the tree.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:29.510
<b>I hope Ichi-nii comes soon.</b>

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:24.100
Things like, "I hope Ichi-nii comes soon,"

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.760
or "I want to get stronger
by the time Ichi-nii arrives,"

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:29.200
and "I want to play with Ichi-nii."

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:34.120
They all just wrote about how much 
they wanted to see their Ichi-nii.

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:41.220
You wanted these wishes to come true, so you
 turned them into protection charms, Yagen?

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.940
Not really, it's just that our 
little brothers insisted.

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:50.810
I see, so you've been taking care 
of our brothers until I arrived.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:54.910
It's not just me. Nakigitsune, 
Namazuo, and Honebami, too.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.090
You did well, Yagen.

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:03.600
You can relax now.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.890
Don't say such stupid things, I'm an adult!

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.580
You're lucky, Ichi-nii.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:21.560
The moon today is the most 
beautiful one we've had.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.620
<b>For Ichi-nii</b>

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.620
<b>Journal</b>

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.980
<i>Who suffers more? The ones doing the 
waiting or the ones making them wait?</i>

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:55.080
<i>It seems I really have kept them waiting.</i>

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.430
That crest...

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.180
It's Ichi-nii's?

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.170
Ichi-nii! It's Ichi-nii!

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:08.270
You have Ichi-nii's bell, 
meaning he's here, right?!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.570
All right!

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:11.070
Where?

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.280
Where is he?

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:14.360
I want to see him, now!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.980
Don't be impatient. 
He'll be here in just a bit.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.250
How soon is "just a bit"?

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:23.060
Hey, how about we all shout, 
"Wah!" when Ichi-nii comes?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.520
That's good! I want to do that!

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:25.700
Ah, he's here!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.160
He's here, he's here, he's here!

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.470
Wah!

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:33.700
What? This is surprising!

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.070
Tsurumaru-san? We made
 a mistake! It's Tsurumaru-san!

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.070
We're sorry!

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.930
That's pretty impressive, 
surprising me like that.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.600
Although, surprises are important in life...

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.790
We apologize, Tsurumaru-sama. 
We mistook you for someone else.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:46.620
With whom?

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:47.510
There!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.470
Isn't that Ichi-nii?

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.870
It's Ichi-nii!

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:54.680
I knew it!

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:55.860
Ichi-nii!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.150
It's Ichi-nii!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.010
Now this <i>is</i> surprising.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.570
Ichi-nii!

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:13.860
Ichi-nii!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.160
Ichi-nii!! We've missed you!

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:21.900
I wanted to play with everyone, 
too, so I made this.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:23.940
Wow! A swing!

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:25.400
Ichi-nii is amazing!

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:28.420
I want to ride it with Ichi-nii!

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:31.370
Me, too! Me, too!

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:31.370
And me!

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.990
Everyone will get a turn. 
We can't all swing on it.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.520
If Ichi-nii holds on to us, it'll be fine!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:37.620
Let's ride!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.440
I want to ride it a bunch!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:44.320
Please ride it, too, Yagen-niisan.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.410
No, I'm fine.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:47.830
Yagen-niisan!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:48.870
Yagen!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.380
Hurry, Yagen-niisan!

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:52.390
Ride with us, Yagen!

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:53.880
Fine.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.580
I'm coming!

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:56.920
Here we go!

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:00.030
Yay!

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:24.030
<b>I want to be with everyone from now on. 
- Ichigo Hitofuri</b>

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:28.030
Hey, hey. Let's have a welcome 
party. Ichi-nii's welcome party!

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:28.990
Good idea!

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:30.010
We want to do it!

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:30.130
I want to do it!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.540
Ichi-nii's welcome party, agreed!

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.070
Agreed.

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:34.820
Okay, but what are we going to do?

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.790
What would you like to do, Ichi-nii?

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:41.100
I am happy with anything, 
as long as I'm with everyone.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.400
If that's the case...

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.760
<b>Just Before the General Election</b>

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:45.610
Let's do this!

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:49.720
There's no <b>fight</b> we can't <b>win</b>

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.720
This kind of group was in 
the magazine I got from Master.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.490
"Idols?"

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.320
They're so shiny!

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:58.760
It seems idols sing and dance while 
wearing cute costumes like these.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:04.030
Idol!

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.230
So cute!

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:07.620
I want to sing!

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:08.990
I want to dance!

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:11.040
So we'll sing and dance for 
Ichi-nii's welcome party?

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:14.920
Hey, let's all sing together!

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:19.230
We'll mimic this group's name: A-Wa-Ta48!

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.290
AWT48?

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:27.300
That's a good idea! I want to sing!

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:30.560
It says that a person called a "producer"
 is necessary for an idol group.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.780
Producer?

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:36.980
Which means, AWT48's producer will be...

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.940
Handed down from the Akimoto Family of 
the Dewa Province in the Yamagata Domain

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.580
I'll sing in the middle of the stage.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.020
That one's called the "center."

00:21:45.020 --> 00:21:46.810
I should be center, then!

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:48.490
I won't give up the center!

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:50.180
The center is definitely me!

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:50.900
Me!

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:51.800
Me, too!

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:52.790
M-Me too!

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.200
I was aiming for it, too.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:58.300
Then let's have the producer decide, 
that way no one will be upset.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.280
Please, Producer.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:06.070
The person with the most 
flair should be the center.

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:35.850
<b>Osaka Castle</b>

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:50.230
Another nightmare about the Ikeda Inn?

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:52.480
AWT48.

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:54.510
Are you okay?

00:23:55.080 --> 00:24:00.070
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
